==Status Report: 2026-10-17 19:07 PDT==
IMPLEMENTED and CLOSED. Added data-transfer-rate units to the units stage
(`Normalizer.UNIT_WORDS`), which already expands "5 km/h" / "80 mph" and guards
each match with `(?<=\d)` so a bare "GB/s" is never touched:

  Gbit/s, Mbit/s, kbit/s  ->  "...bits per second"
  Gbps,   Mbps,   kbps    ->  "...bits per second"   (b = bit)
  GB/s,   MB/s,   kB/s    ->  "...bytes per second"  (B = byte)

so "40 Gbit/s", "20 Gbps", "480 Mbit/s", "500 MB/s", "5 GB/s" read as "40
gigabits per second", "20 gigabits per second", etc. This covers the USB-C
article's "Gbit/s"/"Gbps" transfer rates and its "MB/s"/"GB/s" storage figures.
Matching is case-insensitive like the rest of the units map, so lowercase
"gbps"/"KB/s" spellings also resolve; the bits-vs-bytes "b"/"B" case distinction
is deliberately collapsed (rare in prose).

Verified: `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` passes (new cases in NormalizerTest).
